WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.563
Hi, I'm Kevel!

00:00:02.563 --> 00:00:06.544
One hidden unit inside a language model can change what the whole model writes.

00:00:06.544 --> 00:00:09.673
Here is how you find one, and how hard to push.

00:00:11.058 --> 00:00:14.238
A neuron writes one fixed direction into the residual stream.

00:00:14.238 --> 00:00:17.737
Steering just adds a dose of that direction, scaled by how

00:00:17.737 --> 00:00:19.009
big the stream is.

00:00:20.758 --> 00:00:24.900
Run two sets of prompts through the model and record every neuron's activation.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.461
Rank the neurons by how differently they fire on the two sets.

00:00:28.881 --> 00:00:29.468
Pick one.

00:00:29.468 --> 00:00:32.694
Its column in the down projection is the direction it writes.

00:00:33.114 --> 00:00:36.431
Scale that column by a dose, and add it to the residual

00:00:36.431 --> 00:00:37.537
stream at every position.

00:00:39.108 --> 00:00:40.232
Here is the formula.

00:00:41.108 --> 00:00:42.950
The dose is a fraction of the stream.

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:47.153
Multiply by the median norm of the stream leaving that layer,

00:00:47.153 --> 00:00:48.313
which grows with depth.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:52.918
Divide by the column's own length, to get the shift in the neuron's activation.

00:00:54.608 --> 00:00:57.934
A detector fires when the text is French, and a contrast

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.143
ranking finds it easily.

00:00:59.563 --> 00:01:03.612
A writer adds its column to the stream and changes what comes next.

00:01:03.612 --> 00:01:05.169
Only some detectors are writers.

00:01:06.508 --> 00:01:10.804
Of the ten top ranked neurons, two changed the language of the continuation.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:12.786
None of ten random ones did.

00:01:14.008 --> 00:01:15.252
The window is narrow.

00:01:15.252 --> 00:01:18.983
Between a dose of point one and point one five, perplexity jumps

00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:21.471
twenty two fold, and the text turns French.

00:01:23.058 --> 00:01:24.473
Detecting French is reading.

00:01:24.473 --> 00:01:28.716
Steering is writing, and the dose scale decides whether the text survives.

00:01:30.608 --> 00:01:34.075
A neuron writes one column direction, the dose is a fraction of

00:01:34.075 --> 00:01:36.965
the stream, and a detector is not always a writer.

00:01:37.385 --> 00:01:39.486
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:39.486 --> 00:01:40.086
I'm Kevel.

00:01:40.086 --> 00:01:40.386
Bye!
